  - "mechanistic-interpretability"
  - "pytorch"
abstract: >-
  Richardson Attention (Superconducting Spectral Attention) is a zero-training,
  calibration-guided runtime inference architecture that restores 1-Hop through
  5-Hop compositional reasoning across 8K-12K contexts in pre-trained hybrid
  Sliding-Window/Global-Attention Transformers (validated on google/gemma-4-E2B-it
  and google/gemma-4-E4B-it). By isolating a sparse Global Logic Quorum via
  precision-matrix Variance Inflation Factor (VIF) pruning and applying
  Query-Slice Dual-State Symmetric Boltzmann Extrapolation over a depth-progressive
  Renormalization Group (RG) cubic plateau schedule, Richardson Attention flips
  3-Hop pointer chasing from 0.10% FAIL to 95.87% WIN and 5-Hop pointer chasing
  from 2.24% FAIL to 93.89% WIN (41.9x gain, 103.5x decoy error reduction) with
  zero fine-tuning and zero perplexity degradation.
